<!--
  Desert Light - editor color scheme
  Derived from the Desert (dark) scheme in this plugin, which is a
  transcription of desert.vim by Hans Fugal.
  https://github.com/fugalh/desert.vim

  desert.vim is `set background=dark` and has no light counterpart, so every
  colour here is DERIVED, not transcribed: each hue is its dark sibling pulled
  to roughly 30-40% lightness with hue and role held constant, on a parchment
  ground taken from desert's own sand (#c2bfa5). Comments stay sky blue,
  keywords stay khaki, functions stay green.

  Light palette
    text         2b2a22   parchment    f2f0e6   sand         8a8562
    khaki        8a7d0f   darkkhaki    6f6a1e   navajowhite  9a6a1b
    tan          8a6230   indianred    93372c   softpink     a63030
    skyblue      1c7099   palegreen    22701f   olivedrab    5a7a1e
-->
